\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S.6}{\ignorespaces Raw-fraction variant of Fig.~3 of the article. \textit  {(a)} The upper histograms show the fraction of CG\textsubscript  {4}{} and Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} quartets per 0.1-dex bin, with dotted lines at their medians (143 and 293~kpc). Below, points give raw E-class fractions among E/S satellites in 0.2-dex bins, with 95\% physical-host bootstrap intervals. Bins with fewer than three hosts are omitted. The curves are logistic fits at \(\log _{10}(M_\star /M_\odot )=10.20\). \textit  {(b)} The separate-slope model averages predictions over locally comparable CG\textsubscript  {4}{} satellites. The circle and bar show the estimate at 150~kpc and its pointwise 95\% interval. The ribbon and summary contrasts are as in the article.}}{6}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:supp_compactness_raw}{{S.6}{6}{Raw-fraction variant of Fig.~3 of the article. \textit {(a)} The upper histograms show the fraction of \CG {} and \CC {} quartets per 0.1-dex bin, with dotted lines at their medians (143 and 293~kpc). Below, points give raw E-class fractions among E/S satellites in 0.2-dex bins, with 95\% physical-host bootstrap intervals. Bins with fewer than three hosts are omitted. The curves are logistic fits at \(\log _{10}(M_\star /M_\odot )=10.20\). \textit {(b)} The separate-slope model averages predictions over locally comparable \CG {} satellites. The circle and bar show the estimate at 150~kpc and its pointwise 95\% interval. The ribbon and summary contrasts are as in the article}{figure.6}{}}
